+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create an order and pay for it, but there is no way to reduce the
+amount due before paying. Coupons already exist as data (the `coupons` table and
+the admin endpoints), yet the redemption path - `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` -
+is missing, so discount data on an order can never be filled in.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon`, accepting `{ "couponCode": "..." }` and
+  returning the updated order in the same shape as `GET /orders/:id`.
+- Normalize the incoming code (trim + upper-case) before lookup.
+- Validate the order (exists, `PENDING`, no coupon yet) and the coupon (exists,
+  `ACTIVE`, inside its validity window, usage limit not exhausted, order amount
+  at or above the minimum).
+- Compute the discount for `FIXED` and `PERCENT` coupons, honor the optional
+  per-coupon cap and the order amount as the hard ceiling, and derive
+  `finalAmountCents = amountCents - discount` (never negative).
+- Commit order update, `coupon_redemptions` insert and `used_count` increment in
+  a single transaction that rolls back atomically on any failure.
+- Return the stable `{ "error": { "code", "message" } }` envelope with the
+  prescribed codes and HTTP statuses on rejection, leaving no database writes
+  behind.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupons`: applying a single coupon to a pending order - request
+  normalization, validation order, discount computation, atomic persistence, the
+  response shape, and the rejection contract.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts` gains the new route; `src/services/orderService.ts`
+  gains the rule engine; `src/repositories/` gains the order-update, redemption
+  and usage-count writes.
+- Uses only existing tables (`orders`, `coupons`, `coupon_redemptions`) and the
+  existing injected `Clock`; no schema change, no new dependency.
+- `GET /orders/:id` and the existing order/coupon endpoints keep their current
+  behavior.
+- Adds tests for the new endpoint; existing tests are untouched.
