+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add the order update + redemption insert + `used_count` increment to `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` as one transactional method (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, `COMMIT`, `ROLLBACK` on any error) that re-checks the order is still `PENDING` with no coupon and the coupon's usage limit still holds before writing; verify with `npm run build` and by asserting after a successful call that the order row, one new `coupon_redemptions` row and the incremented `used_count` are all visible.
+- [x] 1.2 Keep the redemption insert and `used_count` increment inside that same transactional method instead of spreading them across repositories, so no transaction ever spans two repositories; verify with `npm run build` that only repositories contain SQL (`rg -n "SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE" src/services src/routes` returns nothing).
+
+## 2. Business rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, body)` in `src/services/orderService.ts`: normalize the code, then run the guard sequence in the exact rejection order from the spec (invalid body → order missing → not pending → already applied → coupon missing → inactive → not yet valid → expired → usage exhausted → minimum not met), all before any write; verify the 400/404/409 codes with tests for each guard.
+- [x] 2.2 Compute the discount (`FIXED` value or `floor(amount * value / 100)`), apply `maxDiscountCents` when non-NULL, then cap at `amountCents` and derive `finalAmountCents = amountCents - discount`; verify the AC-01…AC-05 numbers in tests.
+- [x] 2.3 Read `now` from the injected `Clock` for the window check and the redemption timestamp, never `new Date()`; verify a fixed clock at `validFrom` succeeds and at `validUntil` yields `COUPON_EXPIRED`.
+- [x] 2.4 Return the freshly re-read order so the response deep-equals `GET /orders/:id`; verify by comparing the apply response against a follow-up GET.
+
+## 3. HTTP layer
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, parsing only the id via `parseId` and passing the body through; verify the endpoint returns 200 for a valid request and that the route file still contains no rules or SQL.
+
+## 4. Tests and verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts` covering AC-01…AC-10, each error code and precedence case, and side-effect-free rejections (order fields, `coupon_redemptions` count and `usedCount` unchanged); verify `npm test` passes, including the untouched `tests/orders.test.ts`.
+- [x] 4.2 Confirm `npm run build` and `npm test` both pass with no changes to existing tests or `TASK.md`.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once the review requirements are satisfied.
